3	// Tests of the seed side of the nexus-bench command (DEVDESK-544, NX-02a.10,
4	// story DEVDESK-505), written before the code. They pin down, on the `deps` of
5	// main.go and the harness of main_test.go:
6	//
7	//   - the `seed` subcommand: preflight(OpSeed), then Seed with the SeedDeps built
8	//     from deps (runner, forwarder, copier, clock, store), the descriptor written
9	//     only after a Seed that succeeded;
10	//   - `up` as D-J says: Deploy, EnsureUpstream, Provision, Seed, descriptor with
11	//     the whole data set; nothing is written after a failure;
12	//   - `up` with an upstream URL the bench did not deploy: no EnsureUpstream, no
13	//     Seed, the descriptor of NX-01 (an empty data set), and it says so;
14	//   - the context Seed is given, bounded by Params.Timeout;
15	//   - `status`: the `upstream:` and `dataset:` lines, read only.
16	//
17	// cut-upstream, restore-upstream and reset are NX-02b: nothing here tests them.
18	//
19	// Interpretations the tests fix (the report says them again):
20	//
21	//   - `seed` has no data of its own about Nexus (version, edition, EULA): it
22	//     carries them over from the descriptor of the previous run, and refuses to
23	//     seed when there is none readable (run `up` first). The hosts come from the
24	//     preflight node address, as for `provision`.
25	//   - `seed` takes --rest-host (the admin credentials go there) and no
26	//     --accept-eula.
27	//   - the constructors of the doors (newForwarder, newCopier) run before the
28	//     cluster is touched, so a missing skopeo stops `up` before it deploys; they
29	//     are not built when the seed will not run (custom upstream, status).
30	//   - `status` reads the data set against the descriptor, with the digests of
31	//     the REST listing of docker-hosted and docker-proxy, anonymously.
